%!PS
% SPDX-FileCopyrightText: 2026 EfterScript contributors
% SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
% backend: none
% expect-output: FD,5.EHPu*CER),Dg-(AAoDn~>
% expect-output: the quick brown fox
% Scenario: ASCII85Encode over standard output writes five digits per
% four bytes, one digit more than the bytes of a final partial group
% (the last three bytes give four digits), and closefile ends the data
% with `~>`; the same text read through ASCII85Decode gives the bytes
% back. The first group: `the ` is 0x74686520 = 1953064224, which in
% base 85 is 37 11 12 21 13, that is `FD,5.`. The parentheses in the
% text are escaped in the string below.
% Expect: the base-85 text, then the decoded bytes.
(%stdout) (w) file /ASCII85Encode filter
dup (the quick brown fox) writestring closefile
(\n) print
(FD,5.EHPu*CER\),Dg-\(AAoDn~>) /ASCII85Decode filter
100 string readstring pop =
